{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1118766-kinfolk","id":1118766,"title":"Kinfolk.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-20T17:17:21-07:00","id":1118766,"title":"Kinfolk.","content":"Can normal humans become Kinfolk? I know Kinfolk are the result of a mating between a Garou and a human or a wolf, but is there a possibility to turn a human into Kinfolk, given that they proved themselves useful? I've read in the Children of Gaia revised book a while back, reading through the character's dialogue it mentioned something about freeing orphaned children and making them into kinfolk, which raised a big question mark for me since I have no idea what they meant by that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12188-theexplosivearrow","name":"TheExplosiveArrow","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T17:30:06-07:00","id":1118769,"title":"","content":"Generally, you get to be Kinfolk the same way that you get to be a Garou or Fera, by being born that way. The CoG Revised Tribebook had a rite to turn a human into kin, but it also has a rite that involves having sex with other Garou in Crinos, which is supposed to give control over frenzies but contains no mechanics to this effect, so it is highly suspect. There is a rare, roundabout way to manage something similar - kami can have a power that lets them count as Kinfolk to Garou and/or Fera or types of Fera.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-20T19:13:40-07:00","id":1118794,"title":"","content":"There's almost always a way. Though the default of the game makes it far too much effort/risk to be worth it.<br /> <br /> As noted, CoG: Rev. is not generally considered a good book to look to for this sort of thing. There's a lot of weird in it that never shows up again (for good reasons IMO at least).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-21T11:14:02-07:00","id":1119040,"title":"","content":"I do not really mind the CoG Revised book, and it is canon for Revised. The Rite of the Parted Veil (level Five Mystic Rite) requires two unrelated Garou to witness the adoptee's love of Gaia and a number of successes on an extended test equal to the age of the entity being adopted, so I hardly think that it is terribly unbalanced. I actually like the Rite because it allows people who love the Earth (environmentalists, hippies, pagans, scientists, etc) to become part of the Garou Nation.<br /> <br /> I imagine that the Children of Gaia maintain a couple dozen cults throughout the USA that they use to attract and recruit prospective humans for adoption. I could see the average Cult having one hundred human members and ten Human Kinfolk members. Every year, a few Garou would come around and elevate ten humans from each cult to the status of Human Kinfolk and have them join the larger community of Children of Gaia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-23T03:56:31-07:00","id":1119453,"title":"","content":"Thanks guys, preciate your quick answers!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12188-theexplosivearrow","name":"TheExplosiveArrow","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}